.TH "CODEX-NOTIFY" "1" "November 2026" "arran4/dotfiles" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
codex\-notify \- send a Codex attention notification
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBcodex\-notify [approval|question|complete|attention]\fR
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show a short notification for Codex approval, question, completion or general attention events. This internal libexec hook uses notify\-send, kdialog or macOS osascript when available, falling back to a terminal bell.
.SH NOTES
Normally invoked by Codex hooks, not directly by the user.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
A notification utility is optional. The hook prefers notify-send,
then kdialog, then macOS osascript, and finally a terminal bell.
A graphical session is required for desktop popups.
.SH INTEGRATION
The configured ~/.codex/hooks.json maps PreToolUse request_user_input
to question, PermissionRequest to approval and Stop to complete.
These events invoke ~/.local/libexec/codex-notify. An unrecognised
argument selects a generic attention message. Desktop notifications
are launched asynchronously.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
~/.local/libexec/codex-notify question
~/.local/libexec/codex-notify approval
~/.local/libexec/codex-notify complete
.fi
.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
This is a best-effort notification, not a reliable delivery channel.
Graphical notifier errors are suppressed, and without a working
desktop notifier or writable terminal the hook may appear silent.
Verify the hooks.json entry and notifier availability first.
